Important viva questions
Question	Answer
What is Banker's Algorithm?	A deadlock avoidance algorithm.
Who developed Banker's Algorithm?	Edsger W. Dijkstra.
What is the Need formula?	Need = Maximum − Allocation.
What is a safe sequence?	An order in which all processes can complete safely.
Can multiple safe sequences exist?	Yes.
Does an unsafe state always indicate deadlock?	No.
What is the purpose of the Available vector?	To represent currently available resources.
What happens when a process completes?	Its allocated resources are released.
What is the time complexity?	O(n² × m), where n is processes and m is resource types.
Is Banker's Algorithm prevention or avoidance?	Deadlock avoidance.
